WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:50.384 --> 00:51.385
Look.

00:52.678 --> 00:54.930
Are you being harsh
on Eui-ju intentionally?

00:55.598 --> 00:56.599
What do you mean?

00:57.308 --> 01:01.812
Well, she thinks the reflection letter
and demerits you gave her are unfair.

01:01.896 --> 01:04.106
If this is about the filming incident…

01:04.190 --> 01:05.191
Me?

01:05.858 --> 01:06.859
No, right?

01:07.651 --> 01:09.653
It was just a misunderstanding.

01:13.449 --> 01:14.700
She didn't film us.

01:18.704 --> 01:19.955
Well, what is it then?

01:20.664 --> 01:23.042
Why are you so strict only with her?

01:25.586 --> 01:27.004
I can't tolerate…

01:28.714 --> 01:31.050
the fact that Yeo Eui-ju
got a four in math.

01:34.470 --> 01:35.679
[Gi-jeon] Darn it. [sighs]

01:37.640 --> 01:38.641
Eat some.

01:39.225 --> 01:41.852
Each after-school class
needs five students.

01:41.936 --> 01:42.937
I have four.

01:43.938 --> 01:45.856
Woo-su got ten applications for his.

01:48.359 --> 01:50.402
[amusing music playing]

01:52.488 --> 01:54.281
Wait. You got your glasses.

01:54.365 --> 01:55.866
You finally noticed.

01:55.950 --> 01:56.951
[chuckling] Good for you.

01:57.034 --> 01:59.036
[Da-ju] What the… You found them?

01:59.703 --> 02:02.081
-Where were they?
-Did someone happen to see the flyer?

02:02.873 --> 02:03.958
How much did you pay them?

02:04.917 --> 02:05.918
Didn't have to.

02:06.544 --> 02:07.545
Look at this punk.

02:07.628 --> 02:09.129
They didn't take the reward.

02:09.213 --> 02:10.256
-[Da-ju] Huh?
-Why not?

02:11.215 --> 02:12.216
[Dong-ju] Beats me.

02:13.175 --> 02:15.594
-Damn. They're your saviors.
-[Gi-jeon] Ooh.

02:16.303 --> 02:17.680
Now you need to show some respect.

02:18.597 --> 02:20.349
[Gi-jeon] Oh, you should
show more gratitude

02:20.432 --> 02:23.602
-to bring more blessings to your life.
-That's right, punk. Bow down.

02:23.686 --> 02:26.105
-Or another bird could poop on you.
-That's right.

02:26.188 --> 02:27.314
[laughter]

02:27.398 --> 02:29.358
CHAPTER 15: BLINK TWICE
IF YOU'RE HERE UNDER DURESS

02:29.441 --> 02:31.944
Just hearing Choi Yoon write
makes my heart race. Is it just me?

02:32.027 --> 02:34.864
Si-on's breath hit my sweet spot
from his first appearance.

02:34.947 --> 02:37.241
I wish I were tied up
like the leather watch on Yoon's wrist.

02:37.324 --> 02:39.118
How Tae-ha looks at Yoon is enchanting.

02:43.873 --> 02:45.875
[chuckling]

02:48.544 --> 02:49.670
-Boo!
-[exclaims]

02:49.753 --> 02:51.463
Oh. Hi there. [chuckles]

02:51.547 --> 02:52.923
Hey. What's so funny?

02:53.007 --> 02:55.217
What? Oh… [chuckles]

02:55.301 --> 02:56.760
I started writing a new piece

02:57.386 --> 02:58.679
and it's doing pretty well.

02:58.762 --> 03:00.598
Really? Let me read it.

03:01.307 --> 03:03.517
-It's still too embarrassing. Sorry.
-[scoffs]

03:04.351 --> 03:06.604
You're being too secretive about it.

03:08.480 --> 03:09.773
Is it rated R?

03:09.857 --> 03:11.734
[amusing music playing]

03:11.817 --> 03:15.279
-[chuckles] Of course it isn't.
-[chuckling]

03:18.365 --> 03:21.493
Well, it's not BL, is it?

03:23.078 --> 03:24.371
BL?

03:24.455 --> 03:25.998
Well, you know,

03:26.081 --> 03:27.499
boys in love with each other.

03:29.543 --> 03:31.045
Oh, BL.

03:31.670 --> 03:33.297
Yeah, I've heard of it before.

03:34.131 --> 03:35.132
[sighs]

03:35.758 --> 03:37.968
I don't understand
why people enjoy reading that.

03:40.387 --> 03:41.388
Oh.

03:42.264 --> 03:43.474
Me neither.

03:44.099 --> 03:47.728
I mean, why pair two guys together
instead of a man and a woman?

03:48.687 --> 03:49.939
What's the fun of it?

03:51.649 --> 03:52.816
R-Right?

03:53.734 --> 03:56.153
[chuckling] Yeah, you're right. [chuckles]

03:56.737 --> 03:59.073
Wow. The weather's so nice today.

03:59.698 --> 04:01.367
-Yeah.
-[chuckles]

04:01.450 --> 04:03.452
What do we have for first period?

04:09.291 --> 04:10.709
My dad once told me…

04:12.920 --> 04:15.005
that in moments of difficult choices…

04:15.756 --> 04:18.717
Whoa! Is that your application?

04:19.510 --> 04:21.136
Exactly five!

04:21.220 --> 04:22.763
I've got an elite squad.

04:23.347 --> 04:25.307
Let's do this, star athlete!

04:27.518 --> 04:28.769
Sorry, Mr. Jung.

04:34.108 --> 04:36.485
…what ultimately saves you in the end

04:36.986 --> 04:38.946
is taking the harder path.

04:42.074 --> 04:46.161
Mr. Jung, I really wanted to do
the after-school PE class but then

04:46.787 --> 04:48.122
I got a situation.

04:48.205 --> 04:51.875
If your math teacher is blackmailing you
somehow then blink your eyes twice.

04:54.003 --> 04:55.921
[Woo-su] Turns out
she wants to learn math.

04:56.005 --> 04:57.006
[scoffs]

04:57.089 --> 04:59.842
She wants to improve her score
and I just couldn't ignore it.

05:00.634 --> 05:02.678
-I said that?
-She needs to build on what she's good at,

05:02.761 --> 05:04.596
and her running stats are amazing.

05:05.180 --> 05:07.266
She obviously isn't an athlete.

05:08.517 --> 05:10.978
Can't you see the word "lazy"
written on her face, hmm?

05:11.061 --> 05:12.855
Lazy? I'm not lazy.

05:12.938 --> 05:14.356
I'm super diligent, sir.

05:14.440 --> 05:15.899
How much do you sleep?

05:17.735 --> 05:18.736
Ten hours.

05:21.196 --> 05:23.240
As long as you focus when you're awake.

05:23.741 --> 05:25.242
What's your grade point average?

05:27.870 --> 05:29.246
One.

05:35.502 --> 05:37.087
We should listen to him.

05:39.590 --> 05:40.591
No, Mr. Jung.

05:41.175 --> 05:43.761
It's not like I have a one
in all subjects.

05:56.315 --> 06:00.527
Today we're reading Kim So-wol's poem.
A poem called "Chohon".

06:03.238 --> 06:05.783
INVOCATION

06:06.784 --> 06:08.452
[gentle guitar music playing]

06:08.535 --> 06:10.621
KIM SO-WOL

06:14.708 --> 06:16.585
Let me just recite the poem first.

06:17.252 --> 06:18.879
"O name, shattered into pieces."

06:20.672 --> 06:21.882
[student 1] Bring it on.

06:22.925 --> 06:24.218
[student 2] What the heck?

06:26.011 --> 06:28.180
Why do you think Dong-ju
wouldn't use what I got him?

06:30.390 --> 06:32.226
He probably doesn't want to burden you.

06:33.227 --> 06:36.855
Using it might seem like
he's expecting another gift from you.

06:36.939 --> 06:37.940
You think?

06:41.443 --> 06:43.987
Well, I'll tell him I like him
when I'm 20.

06:44.738 --> 06:45.739
[scoffs]

06:45.823 --> 06:48.283
I doubt your crush on Mr. Yoon
will last that long.

06:48.367 --> 06:51.036
You haven't liked anyone
more than 200 days.

06:51.120 --> 06:52.538
It's different this time.

06:53.413 --> 06:56.583
[inhales sharply]
I have something I wanna ask you.

06:56.667 --> 06:58.335
Why do you like him?

06:58.418 --> 07:00.170
I mean, like, what do you like?

07:00.254 --> 07:02.214
There must be something
other than his looks.

07:03.006 --> 07:04.675
Dong-ju is different.

07:04.758 --> 07:06.093
He's different.

07:08.095 --> 07:11.640
How exactly is he different
from all your exes?

07:12.933 --> 07:15.060
[whimsical music playing]

07:15.144 --> 07:16.145
[sighs]

07:20.524 --> 07:22.317
[Go-ya] I feel bad for him.

07:24.903 --> 07:26.530
-Huh?
-I don't know.

07:27.281 --> 07:28.949
When I look at his face,

07:29.783 --> 07:33.871
it feels like my heart's breaking.

07:33.954 --> 07:37.207
[owl hooting plays]

07:37.708 --> 07:38.709
[inhales sharply]

07:39.376 --> 07:40.794
Fair point. Mmm.

07:40.878 --> 07:43.630
My mom said she also
married my dad out of pity.

07:43.714 --> 07:46.425
But she said you shouldn't
marry someone out of pity

07:46.508 --> 07:48.218
because it's ruined
a lot of women's lives.

07:48.302 --> 07:49.303
[inhales deeply]

07:51.680 --> 07:53.015
[stammers] Uh…

07:54.683 --> 07:59.605
I guess it happens
when you're really in love. [chuckles]

08:00.189 --> 08:02.774
-Right? [chuckles]
-[chuckles] Yeah.

08:04.193 --> 08:06.069
Feeling bad for no reason?

08:07.112 --> 08:09.406
[students chattering, laughing]

08:09.990 --> 08:12.409
-I'm on cleaning duty again.
-[chuckles]

08:15.829 --> 08:17.414
[chattering, laughing stops]

08:17.497 --> 08:18.916
[students] Hello.

08:20.542 --> 08:21.543
Good job today.

08:22.502 --> 08:24.213
-[Eui-ju] Look at that face though.
-Thank you.

08:24.296 --> 08:26.131
Who would possibly feel bad for him?

08:26.215 --> 08:29.176
Stay for your cleaning duty
if you have demerit points.

08:29.843 --> 08:32.888
[Eui-ju] No one at all.
No one in his life! [scoffs]

08:32.971 --> 08:34.473
Dismissed.

08:34.556 --> 08:36.642
[students] Thank you.

08:39.478 --> 08:42.356
I can't say I'm surprised,
but Math is a real freak.

08:42.439 --> 08:44.566
He always gives you demerit points.

08:44.650 --> 08:47.527
And now after-school math class?
What is he, Lucifer?

08:48.904 --> 08:50.864
Are you sure you won't take it with me?

08:52.699 --> 08:55.160
You know I would go with you
all the way to hell.

08:56.453 --> 08:58.580
-But after-school math?
-[sighs]

08:58.664 --> 08:59.873
He sure is a genius,

08:59.957 --> 09:02.793
seeing how he punishes someone
with her worst nightmare, right?

09:04.461 --> 09:06.463
Hey, girls. Are you busy today?

09:06.546 --> 09:08.257
-Not really.
-No.

09:08.340 --> 09:09.341
Why?

09:09.424 --> 09:12.219
I have cleaning duty because of demerits
and after-school class.

09:12.302 --> 09:14.137
-Why?
-Uh…

09:15.180 --> 09:17.724
There's something
I've always wanted to do in Korea.

09:17.808 --> 09:19.393
-What?
-What is it?

09:19.476 --> 09:22.145
-What is it?
-[giggles]

09:22.229 --> 09:24.523
CHAPTER 16:
MATH IS ABOUT PERSEVERANCE

09:36.576 --> 09:37.577
[sighs]

09:38.161 --> 09:39.162
[comical music playing]

09:39.246 --> 09:40.580
[Eui-ju] Mr. Jung.

09:40.664 --> 09:44.501
I guess I'm destined
to only look at you from far away.

09:45.460 --> 09:48.380
[sighs] Is this crushing pain I feel

09:48.463 --> 09:50.549
because of our star-crossed love?

09:51.049 --> 09:54.094
[whines] Why is fate being so cruel to us?

09:54.803 --> 09:57.222
Hi there. Need anything?

09:58.557 --> 10:00.225
Mr. Ga made you do it?

10:01.643 --> 10:02.728
Unbelievable.

10:03.478 --> 10:04.479
No.

10:05.063 --> 10:06.982
Uh, let me help you.

10:07.065 --> 10:08.233
It's okay. It's okay.

10:09.318 --> 10:10.319
It's fine.

10:12.237 --> 10:13.238
Oh. [chuckles]

10:13.905 --> 10:14.990
It's fine.

10:15.073 --> 10:16.074
Thanks.

10:20.037 --> 10:21.621
You do have potential.

10:21.705 --> 10:22.998
I'm not just saying that.

10:25.417 --> 10:27.127
Ask me, if you have any questions.

10:27.878 --> 10:29.463
And if you need anything.

10:30.380 --> 10:31.381
Yes, sir.

10:31.465 --> 10:33.717
[gentle guitar music playing]

10:35.969 --> 10:36.970
Well…

10:37.763 --> 10:41.266
Mr. Jung, you used to compete
in luge singles,

10:41.350 --> 10:45.896
but then you had to quit after
fracturing your left shin, is that right?

10:46.980 --> 10:48.190
How did you know that?

10:49.066 --> 10:50.359
I read it on the news.

10:51.943 --> 10:53.528
It doesn't affect my life.

10:53.612 --> 10:56.823
Still, you made it to fourth place
in the Winter Games.

10:56.907 --> 10:59.034
-It must've felt bad having to quit.
-[sighs]

11:00.494 --> 11:03.789
Do you think I feel bad
for not winning a medal?

11:07.959 --> 11:09.086
[sighs]

11:09.169 --> 11:11.254
There's something
that matters more than that.

11:12.089 --> 11:15.258
When I was watching the winners
from down there, below the podium,

11:15.342 --> 11:16.426
I came to think

11:17.844 --> 11:21.848
that they probably trained and struggled
harder than I did for those Winter Games.

11:23.475 --> 11:25.268
It seriously felt like dying.

11:26.812 --> 11:28.563
It must've been the same for everyone.

11:36.321 --> 11:38.448
That's when I stopped caring
about the rankings.

11:40.242 --> 11:41.451
And most of all…

11:45.956 --> 11:47.833
I kept the promise to myself.

11:50.836 --> 11:51.962
I didn't give up.

11:52.838 --> 11:53.839
That's what matters.

11:57.801 --> 11:59.636
[Eui-ju] If I'd taken after-school PE,

11:59.719 --> 12:02.389
I could've had more time to talk
and be closer to him.

12:03.974 --> 12:05.559
If it wasn't for Math…

12:05.642 --> 12:07.060
[phone buzzing]

12:13.567 --> 12:15.193
-Hello?
-Where are you?

12:17.320 --> 12:19.448
Come to the office
and get the printouts for class.

12:19.531 --> 12:20.532
[stammers]

12:21.283 --> 12:24.035
Can't you ask someone else to do it?
Ask Eun Ha-su.

12:24.119 --> 12:25.662
You're the president of the math class.

12:25.745 --> 12:27.706
-Since when?
-You have three minutes.

12:31.585 --> 12:33.420
I need to go, Mr. Jung.

12:33.503 --> 12:35.130
-You're leaving?
-Yes.

12:35.213 --> 12:36.214
Goodbye.

12:43.180 --> 12:46.391
That girl is the top student in her class.

12:46.475 --> 12:49.394
And she's the top student in her class.

12:49.478 --> 12:51.480
This class is for all the top students.

12:52.105 --> 12:54.316
I'm not supposed to be here at all.

13:06.786 --> 13:08.205
Are you here to hand this out?

13:12.042 --> 13:14.544
No, I'm in this class too.

13:14.628 --> 13:16.963
You are? Why?

13:18.590 --> 13:20.217
Mr. Ga told me to.

13:20.717 --> 13:22.093
Our homeroom teacher?

13:23.220 --> 13:24.971
Maybe he just did it
so we would save time.

13:25.555 --> 13:27.516
It's kinda nice to have an errand girl.

13:28.517 --> 13:29.559
You think?

13:29.643 --> 13:31.811
[chuckles] I guess that's true.

13:31.895 --> 13:33.897
I hear she got a four on the mock exam.

13:33.980 --> 13:35.398
[student] A four?

13:37.359 --> 13:38.360
[Ha-su] Yep.

13:38.443 --> 13:40.111
[chuckles]

14:13.144 --> 14:15.146
[funky music playing]

14:17.774 --> 14:19.234
[Eui-ju gasps]

14:28.785 --> 14:30.912
-Where are you going?
-Mr. Ga.

14:31.538 --> 14:33.540
Could I just not take this class?

14:33.623 --> 14:36.918
I think that this class
is way above my math level.

14:37.002 --> 14:41.464
My older cousin and my tutor once told me
that I wasn't cut out for math at all,

14:41.548 --> 14:42.632
and they were actually right.

14:42.716 --> 14:45.135
I'm hopeless with numbers.

14:45.218 --> 14:47.262
Unlike subjects you can memorize,

14:47.345 --> 14:51.308
my math score isn't going to improve
just because I put more effort into it.

14:53.143 --> 14:54.477
Why four?

14:54.561 --> 14:56.146
Did you just guess the answers?

14:57.022 --> 14:58.648
I solved the problems.

14:59.524 --> 15:01.943
[rock music playing]

15:18.627 --> 15:19.628
Exactly.

15:19.711 --> 15:21.880
When Gauss was approximating
the number of primes,

15:21.963 --> 15:24.758
he spent years manually finding
every single prime up to three million.

15:24.841 --> 15:27.844
Math's about perseverance,
and you've got perseverance.

15:27.927 --> 15:30.555
-Now get in there.
-[whimpers] But Mr. Ga…

15:31.348 --> 15:35.352
[Woo-su] Given that angle CFA

15:35.435 --> 15:38.146
equals angle CAF,

15:38.229 --> 15:41.733
AC equals CF, which equals 14.

15:42.734 --> 15:43.735
Now solve the problem.

15:54.871 --> 15:56.164
[sighs]

16:00.001 --> 16:02.712
What the heck?
Why is she putting on makeup?

16:03.296 --> 16:04.673
In the middle of class.

16:05.465 --> 16:06.466
No way!

16:06.549 --> 16:08.176
[intriguing music playing]

16:08.259 --> 16:09.260
Dang!

16:10.136 --> 16:11.680
Of course she would.

16:11.763 --> 16:14.974
She has a crush on Math?
[chuckling] Crazy!

16:22.607 --> 16:26.319
[groans] When am I
going to work on the third episode?

16:37.622 --> 16:39.749
-Yeo Eui-ju!
-Huh?

16:40.500 --> 16:41.501
Yes.

16:41.584 --> 16:43.586
What about the third episode?

16:45.213 --> 16:46.715
The third episode?

16:47.215 --> 16:49.759
Yes. Tell me, how does it go?

16:51.720 --> 16:54.431
[playful music playing]

16:56.850 --> 16:57.851
Uh,

16:58.435 --> 17:01.062
the readers might expect that

17:01.146 --> 17:05.817
Yoon will pay off the $6,000
in the third episode.

17:07.444 --> 17:10.363
The real highlight of episode three
is that heart-fluttering scene

17:10.447 --> 17:12.157
between Si-on and Yoon.

17:12.240 --> 17:13.950
They're studying together
at Si-on's place,

17:14.033 --> 17:16.327
and that's when Si-on goes…

17:17.454 --> 17:20.039
"Oh, you're truly cruel."

17:20.123 --> 17:22.459
"You keep pushing me to have dark ideas."

17:22.542 --> 17:23.543
He says that to Yoon.

17:24.127 --> 17:27.338
And then Yoon answers by saying,
"Stop joking around."

17:27.422 --> 17:29.716
And then Si-on answers by saying,

17:29.799 --> 17:33.219
"Do I look like I'm joking?
I'm always honest with you!"

17:33.303 --> 17:35.263
I'm always honest with you.

17:36.222 --> 17:37.223
[giggling]

17:57.535 --> 18:00.580
Finish the problems we covered today
by tomorrow.

18:01.414 --> 18:03.041
By… By tomorrow?

18:07.921 --> 18:10.173
Darn it. [clicks tongue]

18:10.256 --> 18:14.719
CHAPTER 17:
(JUST A MARVELOUS TEACHER)

18:14.803 --> 18:17.430
[Jenny] There's something
I've always wanted to do in Korea!

18:17.514 --> 18:19.265
GUESTHOUSE

18:19.349 --> 18:21.893
A pajama party!

18:28.650 --> 18:30.360
-Eui-ju!
-[Yeong-jae] It's Eui-ju!

18:30.443 --> 18:33.363
[Go-ya] Hey! What took you so long?
What were you up to?

18:33.446 --> 18:34.906
Is this where I can find the famous

18:34.989 --> 18:36.783
-and amazing fortune teller?
-Oh, come on.

18:36.866 --> 18:39.244
Oh, of course.
Come on and have a seat please.

18:39.327 --> 18:41.204
-Is your name Yeo Eui-ju?
-Yes.

18:41.287 --> 18:42.413
-Sit down with us.
-Hello.

18:42.497 --> 18:43.832
What took you so long?

18:44.791 --> 18:46.626
This is for you. Welcome!

18:46.709 --> 18:48.670
-Aw, Eui-ju.
-[Go-ya] Hey, what about us?

18:48.753 --> 18:51.047
-You're so sweet!
-You don't have one for me?

18:51.130 --> 18:53.466
-It's so adorable!
-It's so cute!

18:53.550 --> 18:55.176
-I'm jealous.
-Thank you.

18:55.260 --> 18:56.553
Wow, you ate all that?

18:56.636 --> 18:57.929
-It was a piece of cake.
-Yes.

18:58.012 --> 18:59.722
Thus spoke Kim Dan-ji.

18:59.806 --> 19:02.392
Eat like there's no tomorrow!

19:02.475 --> 19:04.269
-[friends laugh]
-I'm so full.

19:04.769 --> 19:06.229
-[friends gasp]
-[Jenny] Wow.

19:06.312 --> 19:07.689
-What is it?
-That's a must!

19:07.772 --> 19:08.982
We gotta eat this for sure.

19:09.065 --> 19:11.317
Wait a sec. Let me make
some space for it. Hold on.

19:11.401 --> 19:13.528
-We always have a space for dessert!
-That's rice cake sticks,

19:13.611 --> 19:16.030
-and those, sweet potatoes.
-Let's go to the kitchen together.

19:16.114 --> 19:18.241
-Everyone to the grill!
-Let's go!

19:18.324 --> 19:20.076
-Off you go!
-Eui-ju, change into this first.

19:20.159 --> 19:22.871
-Oh! The outfit!
-Let's go, let's go, let's go!

19:22.954 --> 19:24.414
[Dan-ji] Jenny, medium, well done.

19:24.497 --> 19:26.457
And now, let's see…

19:26.541 --> 19:28.543
[gasps] Wow.

19:29.168 --> 19:31.462
-Huh?
-[Eui-ju] You roast them all in there.

19:31.546 --> 19:35.425
[exclaims] And now, I'll show you
the true taste of Korean food.

19:35.508 --> 19:38.595
-Ooh, yay! I'm so excited.
-So excited!

19:38.678 --> 19:41.180
-Smells good, right?
-Yes.

19:41.264 --> 19:43.266
Wow. It's really warm.

19:43.349 --> 19:44.392
I know, right?

19:46.769 --> 19:48.730
Wh-What? Need something?

19:49.856 --> 19:50.857
Uh…

19:53.109 --> 19:55.445
J-Jenny, by any chance…

19:55.528 --> 19:57.447
[clears throat, clicks tongue]

19:57.530 --> 19:59.782
…do you know a story called
A Night in Paris?

19:59.866 --> 20:01.117
A NIGHT IN PARIS

20:01.868 --> 20:03.995
Oh, do you know that novel too?

20:05.496 --> 20:08.207
Yeah, that used to be my favorite novel.

20:08.291 --> 20:11.669
In the novel,
the female protagonist, Isabelle,

20:11.753 --> 20:14.964
meets her Brazilian boyfriend in Paris.
At the Louvre, you know?

20:15.048 --> 20:17.592
I had a hunch
when I saw your username. [chuckles]

20:17.675 --> 20:20.178
And then you said
the lines from the novel.

20:21.304 --> 20:22.305
[chuckles]

20:22.889 --> 20:24.933
So you knew it, didn't you?

20:25.642 --> 20:26.935
That I was just lying?

20:27.977 --> 20:31.731
Oh, come on. Everyone wants to be
the main character in a novel, right?

20:31.814 --> 20:34.776
I just figured you were
a huge fan of that novel.

20:36.194 --> 20:38.112
I don't even have a boyfriend.

20:38.196 --> 20:40.448
Everything I know about romance
is from books.

20:41.157 --> 20:43.034
[chuckles] Yeah.

20:43.117 --> 20:44.994
Well, there's nothing wrong with that.

20:45.078 --> 20:46.621
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

20:48.122 --> 20:50.792
[giggles] At first,
I read the translated versions.

20:50.875 --> 20:52.794
But I wanted to read
the original version so much

20:52.877 --> 20:55.713
that I thought
I should just learn English.

20:56.297 --> 21:00.635
Geez. So, your English is this good
just from reading novels?

21:01.135 --> 21:04.847
Well, I read them so many times
that I memorized the lines.

21:04.931 --> 21:06.224
-Oh.
-[chuckles]

21:07.016 --> 21:09.519
So then, do you read romance novels too?

21:09.602 --> 21:11.854
Well, I guess that…

21:12.355 --> 21:15.108
I started with modern romance, you know.

21:15.191 --> 21:18.820
But then I kinda
got into overseas romances.

21:18.903 --> 21:20.196
And then after that…

21:22.991 --> 21:24.450
Then what?

21:26.244 --> 21:28.204
Well, anyway, uh…

21:28.287 --> 21:30.707
Modern romance is pretty much
the mainstream, you know.

21:30.790 --> 21:33.918
-[chuckles]
-Mm-hmm. You're right, you're right.

21:34.002 --> 21:37.630
Reading romance novels
totally gave me this Korea fantasy too.

21:38.297 --> 21:41.467
-Oh, so that's what happened.
-[giggles]

21:41.551 --> 21:43.636
Wait, then what else do you like?

21:43.720 --> 21:45.763
[joyful pop music playing]

21:45.847 --> 21:47.807
[Jenny] Fifty Shades of Mr. CEO.

21:47.890 --> 21:50.018
-Have you heard of it?
-[gasps] Of course! Did you read it?

21:50.101 --> 21:52.478
Yes! [squeals] Did you read it too?

21:52.562 --> 21:54.313
-Yeah, of course.
-It was so good, right?

21:54.397 --> 21:57.108
-Wow, this one's so well roasted.
-This is so good.

21:57.900 --> 21:59.402
-What about it?
-Yeah, it's good, right?

21:59.485 --> 22:00.862
-This is so well roasted.
-Try it.

22:00.945 --> 22:02.155
I know, right? Try a bite.

22:02.780 --> 22:04.198
Oh, no. Hold on a sec.

22:04.282 --> 22:06.200
Wait. Yeah, yeah,
that's what I wanted to do.

22:06.784 --> 22:09.454
A roasted sweet potato
must have some kimchi on top.

22:09.537 --> 22:10.538
Open wide.

22:11.497 --> 22:13.666
-[Jenny] Mmm.
-[Dan-ji] I'm jealous.

22:13.750 --> 22:16.127
-What do you think? Like it?
-Wow.

22:16.210 --> 22:17.712
-Isn't it delicious?
-JMT!

22:17.795 --> 22:20.298
-[laughing]
-Delish!

22:20.381 --> 22:21.966
Wait. Where? Where?

22:22.050 --> 22:23.051
Really?

22:23.134 --> 22:25.970
-Stop it, stop it. Ah, stop.
-Come here.

22:26.054 --> 22:28.264
Jenny, come here.
You need some on your face too.

22:30.266 --> 22:31.476
It's like honey.

22:31.559 --> 22:33.102
Its like honey, yeah.

22:33.186 --> 22:34.771
How is it? Isn't it delicious?

22:34.854 --> 22:36.064
-Good, right?
-What do you think?

22:36.147 --> 22:37.565
Mmm. It's delicious too.

22:37.648 --> 22:39.150
[giggling]

22:39.233 --> 22:40.359
[all sigh]

22:42.320 --> 22:43.738
Dang, I'm so full.

22:44.989 --> 22:46.657
There are a whole lot of stars.

22:50.161 --> 22:51.579
There are so many of us, right?

22:51.662 --> 22:52.872
[giggling]

22:52.955 --> 22:57.168
Remember when Math said that
we're all like stars in the universe?

22:57.251 --> 22:59.420
[giggling]

22:59.504 --> 23:03.424
[Go-ya] Well, in a way,
Math is kind of like the Little Prince,

23:03.508 --> 23:05.009
don't you think?

23:05.093 --> 23:08.679
You know, there's my own shining star
somewhere up in the sky.

23:08.763 --> 23:10.848
And that star is reaching out
to talk to me.

23:10.932 --> 23:12.433
Did you do your homework?

23:12.517 --> 23:13.559
[screams, gasps]

23:13.643 --> 23:15.394
-What?
-What is it?

23:16.395 --> 23:17.396
[groans]

23:18.147 --> 23:20.066
I have math homework to do.

23:20.691 --> 23:22.819
Ah, darn that math homework.

23:22.902 --> 23:26.155
Come on! I barely got to have any fun
because of that after-school class.

23:26.239 --> 23:27.949
When am I even supposed to do it?

23:28.032 --> 23:30.785
-I don't wanna do it. I really don't.
-[chuckles]

23:30.868 --> 23:33.121
You might get demerit points again
if you don't do it.

23:33.204 --> 23:35.540
[groans] I don't wanna.

23:36.374 --> 23:37.875
What should you do?

23:37.959 --> 23:39.210
[sobs] I don't know.

23:39.293 --> 23:41.587
Whatever. I'm skipping it.
I'm not doing it.

23:41.671 --> 23:44.841
Oh, Eui-ju, you've got some guts.

23:44.924 --> 23:46.926
Did you see Math's face
when she faked being sick?

23:47.009 --> 23:48.094
Yeah, I remember.

23:48.177 --> 23:50.304
You could see the anger
burning in his eyes.

23:50.972 --> 23:56.227
CHAPTER 18: STRANGELY FAMILIAR,
ALMOST MATHEMATICAL

24:05.278 --> 24:06.320
Mr. Ga.

24:06.404 --> 24:10.616
[stammers] I couldn't do my homework.

24:10.700 --> 24:13.119
Can I write them out ten times instead?

24:13.202 --> 24:14.453
Did you try to solve them?

24:17.540 --> 24:19.834
Try to solve at least one by yourself.

24:19.917 --> 24:21.586
Just like how you solved the mock exam.

24:22.795 --> 24:24.130
It doesn't work like that.

24:24.213 --> 24:26.591
Not everything works by just trying.

24:28.259 --> 24:29.260
Yeo Eui-ju.

24:30.636 --> 24:31.637
Yes?

24:31.721 --> 24:34.098
What did I say math was on my first day?

24:40.188 --> 24:41.272
The universe.

24:44.317 --> 24:45.318
Euclid?

24:45.401 --> 24:47.028
In here, not in the classroom.

24:47.945 --> 24:48.946
Ah…

24:50.615 --> 24:51.949
Uh…

24:56.245 --> 24:57.830
It's a subject that requires thought.

24:57.914 --> 24:58.915
Ah.

25:00.208 --> 25:01.209
Right.

25:01.292 --> 25:03.794
You probably weren't paying attention,
just like right now.

25:08.090 --> 25:10.843
I was hoping you'd actually try
to solve at least one problem.

25:12.887 --> 25:15.181
I didn't realize
you were such a lost cause.

25:18.476 --> 25:19.852
I'm disappointed.

25:33.824 --> 25:35.034
I'm really sorry.

25:48.214 --> 25:50.925
He's disappointed in me?
What was he expecting?

25:52.885 --> 25:54.887
He's making me feel sorry for nothing.

25:58.766 --> 26:00.685
At least I got some lines I can use.

26:06.899 --> 26:09.235
So, how did he pay back those $6,000?

26:09.318 --> 26:11.529
Don't keep all the good stuff
only to yourself, huh?

26:11.612 --> 26:13.823
Did the writer pass out
in the middle of writing or something?

26:13.906 --> 26:14.991
Give me episode three!

26:15.074 --> 26:17.743
Episode three! Episode three!
Episode three!

26:18.786 --> 26:20.705
Okay, Mr. Ga's lines.

26:21.622 --> 26:22.873
[muttering]

26:22.957 --> 26:24.667
I DIDN'T REALIZE YOU WERE SUCH…

26:26.294 --> 26:30.673
I'M VERY DISAPPOINTED, YOON

26:32.133 --> 26:34.385
[Si-on] I didn't realize
you were such a lost cause.

26:34.927 --> 26:37.096
I'm very disappointed, Yoon.

26:39.724 --> 26:40.725
What is it?

26:45.438 --> 26:47.565
How can you be reading in this situation?

26:49.400 --> 26:50.985
-[tapping keys]
-[chuckles]

26:51.068 --> 26:52.653
-Stop joking around.
-[inhales sharply]

26:53.612 --> 26:56.324
Did Kang Tae-ha say
he'd wait in front of your house again?

26:57.074 --> 26:58.159
YOON'S PAUSE INCENSES SI-ON

26:58.242 --> 26:59.243
I don't know.

27:00.286 --> 27:01.495
You're truly cruel.

27:04.415 --> 27:06.250
You keep pushing me to have dark ideas.

27:06.334 --> 27:08.044
[chuckles]

27:08.127 --> 27:10.129
I love it when you look at me, lying down.

27:10.212 --> 27:12.465
Every time you do,
I just wanna shut you up with my lips.

27:12.548 --> 27:14.508
Until you're out of breath.
[breathing shakily]

27:14.592 --> 27:16.469
SI-ON PRESSED AGAINST YOON,
HIS BREATHING RAGGED

27:18.596 --> 27:20.097
[chuckling]

27:25.186 --> 27:26.479
[taps on keyboard]

27:26.562 --> 27:29.273
[exhales deeply, inhales sharply]

27:29.357 --> 27:31.776
That's what I call a cliff-hanger!

27:31.859 --> 27:34.445
No way anyone's skipping next episode.

27:35.154 --> 27:36.989
[smacks lips, sighs]

27:37.073 --> 27:38.074
[chuckles]

27:38.157 --> 27:40.618
[inhales deeply, sighs]

27:43.579 --> 27:44.872
[sniffing]

27:46.624 --> 27:47.625
Huh?

27:48.125 --> 27:50.795
[sniffs] This doesn't

27:50.878 --> 27:54.298
-smell like the library at all.
-[curious music playing]

27:54.382 --> 27:55.966
[sniffing] Huh?

27:56.675 --> 27:59.595
But it's strangely familiar.
How should I put it…

27:59.678 --> 28:03.140
It smells like a skin product
of someone with a nasty temper.

28:03.224 --> 28:06.227
[sniffs] It's kind of like…

28:06.977 --> 28:08.979
mathematical?

28:10.981 --> 28:12.191
Nah.

28:13.818 --> 28:15.277
Uh, nah.

28:15.361 --> 28:17.613
[chuckles] I must be mistaken.

28:17.696 --> 28:19.490
[shakily] Yeah, I must be.

28:20.366 --> 28:23.327
[shudders] Calm down, Eui-ju.

28:24.286 --> 28:25.996
It's probably nothing.

28:26.080 --> 28:28.165
It has to be nothing.

28:28.249 --> 28:31.043
[whimpers, inhales shakily]

28:34.338 --> 28:37.466
[thunderclap]

28:37.550 --> 28:40.594
[tense music playing]

28:42.304 --> 28:43.472
[gasps]

28:44.640 --> 28:45.641
[thunderclap]

28:46.976 --> 28:48.727
-Move!
-[gasps]

28:48.811 --> 28:50.479
Stay right there, Yeo Eui-ju!

28:51.355 --> 28:52.523
I mean…

28:55.025 --> 28:56.026
I…

28:57.236 --> 28:58.237
muk.
